{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_8476321273f84dcf8a316ae1","type":"tool_result","content":"1045\t(deftest set-effect-order-and-collision-trace-test\n1046\t  \"RULING 3 test 5 (B4): the dynamic set's own effect trace -- tap events\n1047\t   in the canonical element order (derived independently below), every\n1048\t   occurrence evaluated exactly once (the two colliding expressions both\n1049\t   appear), and the collided value kept once in the result.\"\n1050\t  (let [n 1\n1051\t        elements [(list 'tap :s1)\n1052\t                  (list 'tap (list '- 'n 1))\n1053\t                  (list 'tap (list '- 1 'n))\n1054\t                  2]\n1055\t        element-root (fn [e] [(root-of (yang/compile-form e false {}))])\n1056\t        ordered (sort-by element-root jing/canonical-compare elements)\n1057\t        ;; the recorded tap argument of each element; the bare literal 2\n1058\t        ;; carries no tap, so it never logs (it still holds its canonical\n1059\t        ;; position between the tapped elements)\n1060\t        arg-value {(list 'tap :s1) :s1\n1061\t                   (list 'tap (list '- 'n 1)) 0\n1062\t                   (list 'tap (list '- 1 'n)) 0}\n1063\t        expected (into [] (comp (map (fn [e] (get arg-value e ::untapped)))\n1064\t                                (remove #(= % ::untapped)))\n1065\t                       ordered)\n1066\t        traces (trace-of (into #{} elements) {'n n})]\n1067\t    (is (= 3 (count expected)))\n1068\t    (is (= 2 (count (filter #{0} expected)))\n1069\t        \"both colliding occurrences are in the expected trace\")\n1070\t    (doseq [[lane {:keys [value log]}] traces]\n1071\t      (is (= expected log)\n1072\t          (str lane \" consumes the elements in canonical order, each once\"))\n1073\t      (is (= #{:s1 0 2} value)\n1074\t          (str lane \" keeps the collided value once\")))))\n1075\t\n1076\t\n1077\t(deftest colliding-keys-canonical-winner-test\n1078\t  \"RULING 2: for equal evaluated keys the later pair wins, and which pair\n1079\t   is later is the canonical order -- so both insertion orders agree, and\n1080\t   the winner is the one the independent comparator puts last.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"5fa4de0b-7bab-4562-9595-8ec6f9c0e022","timestamp":"2026-11-19T18:09:43.020Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc","content":"(deftest set-effect-order-and-collision-trace-test\n  \"RULING 3 test 5 (B4): the dynamic set's own effect trace -- tap events\n   in the canonical element order (derived independently below), every\n   occurrence evaluated exactly once (the two colliding expressions both\n   appear), and the collided value kept once in the result.\"\n  (let [n 1\n        elements [(list 'tap :s1)\n                  (list 'tap (list '- 'n 1))\n                  (list 'tap (list '- 1 'n))\n                  2]\n        element-root (fn [e] [(root-of (yang/compile-form e false {}))])\n        ordered (sort-by element-root jing/canonical-compare elements)\n        ;; the recorded tap argument of each element; the bare literal 2\n        ;; carries no tap, so it never logs (it still holds its canonical\n        ;; position between the tapped elements)\n        arg-value {(list 'tap :s1) :s1\n                   (list 'tap (list '- 'n 1)) 0\n                   (list 'tap (list '- 1 'n)) 0}\n        expected (into [] (comp (map (fn [e] (get arg-value e ::untapped)))\n                                (remove #(= % ::untapped)))\n                       ordered)\n        traces (trace-of (into #{} elements) {'n n})]\n    (is (= 3 (count expected)))\n    (is (= 2 (count (filter #{0} expected)))\n        \"both colliding occurrences are in the expected trace\")\n    (doseq [[lane {:keys [value log]}] traces]\n      (is (= expected log)\n          (str lane \" consumes the elements in canonical order, each once\"))\n      (is (= #{:s1 0 2} value)\n          (str lane \" keeps the collided value once\")))))\n\n\n(deftest colliding-keys-canonical-winner-test\n  \"RULING 2: for equal evaluated keys the later pair wins, and which pair\n   is later is the canonical order -- so both insertion orders agree, and\n   the winner is the one the independent comparator puts last.\"","numLines":36,"startLine":1045,"totalLines":1550}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_8476321273f84dcf8a316ae1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
