{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261120020943050aa8d671184629","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed the r3 form. Now rewrite it with distinct labels + the mutation counter-check. The new design:\n\n```clojure\n(deftest set-effect-order-and-collision-trace-test\n  \"RULING 3 test 5 (B4): the dynamic set's own effect trace -- tap events\n   in the canonical element order (derived independently below), every\n   occurrence evaluated exactly once (the two colliding expressions carry\n   DISTINCT labels so a swap or duplication cannot hide in the trace),\n   and the collided value kept once in the result.\"\n  (let [n 1\n        ;; distinct labels, one value: each colliding element taps its own\n        ;; label for the trace and returns 0 -- r4: the r3 form tapped the\n        ;; colliding VALUE, so swapping or duplicating the compiled\n        ;; operands was invisible (reviewer probe)\n        left (list 'do (list 'tap :left) (list '- 'n 1))\n        right (list 'do (list 'tap :right) (list '- 1 'n))\n        elements [(list 'tap :s1) left right 2]\n        element-root (fn [e] [(root-of (yang/compile-form e false {}))])\n        ordered (sort-by element-root jing/canonical-compare elements)\n        label-of {(list 'tap :s1) :s1, left :left, right :right}\n        expected (into [] (comp (map (fn [e] (get label-of e ::untapped)))\n                                (remove #(= % ::untapped)))\n                       ordered)\n        form (into #{} elements)\n        ast (yang/compile form)\n        ;; the compiled operands of the colliding elements, for the\n        ;; mutation counter-check below\n        left-node ... right-node ...\n        traces (trace-ast-on ast {'n n})]\n    ...))\n```\n\nFor the mutation check I need the compiled operand NODES. The elements compile to subtrees containing the literal :left / :right (tap's argument). Extract from the constructor: `(first (collection-applications ast))` → operands (after seed). Find operands containing the label: a helper `(fn [ctor label] (some #(when (tree-contains-label? % label) %) (rest (:operands ctor))))`. tree-contains: walk/postwalk looking for `{:type :literal :value label}`.\n\nThen:\n- swap-ast = postwalk-replace {left-node right-node, right-node left-node} on the WHOLE ast (only the set ctor holds them) — the emitted vector order unchanged, but the two SUBTREES exchange positions → the trace becomes [.. :right .. :left ..] i.e. reversed pair → differs from expected ✓.\n- dup-ast = postwalk-replace {right-node left-node} → right replaced by a copy of left → trace has :left twice → differs from expected (missing :right) and the exactly-once property is violated ✓.\n\nRun trace-ast-on for both mutants (walker lane is enough? The reviewer's probe ran all four; do all four for the swap and dup — cheap: each is one small program run ×4 lanes). Assert `(not= expected log)` for each mutant/lane, and specifically the duplicated case's log has 2× :left 0× :right.\n\nWait — trace-of vs trace-ast-on: the mutants are prebuilt ASTs → trace-ast-on. The original: I can use trace-of (compiles the form) or trace-ast-on ast — equivalent; use trace-ast-on ast for symmetry (same machinery as mutants).\n\nAlso `postwalk-replace` uses `=` — the nodes are maps; = works structurally. left-node/right-node are distinct ✓. Replacing within THEMSELVES: postwalk-replace walks and replaces — replacing left-node with right-node INSIDE... the nodes don't nest each other ✓.\n\nOne concern: does `postwalk-replace {left-node right-node right-node left-node}` do a simultaneous swap? It walks and for each form checks (smap form) — a map lookup with the form as key — replaces left→right AND right→left in one pass ✓ (both keys present during the walk).\n\nAlso keep the `(is (= #{:s1 0 2} value))` per route for the ORIGINAL.\n\nAnd the final-value assertion for mutants? The reviewer noted the result set stayed the same in each case — that's fine, the TRACE is the discriminator. Keep mutant assertions to the trace.\n\nAssertion counts: original 4 lanes ×2; mutants 4 lanes ×2 (differs + specific). Let me write it. Also `do` special form — `(list 'do ...)` compiles via compile-do ✓ portable.\n\nDerivation check: expected labels = canonical order of the four element roots with untapped 2 dropped. Per the reviewer's JVM probe: `[:s1 :left :right]` — s1 root < left-do-root < right-do-root < ? where does 2 sit? Doesn't matter (untapped, dropped). My derivation reproduces [:s1 :left :right] on JVM. Then swap → [:s1 :right :left], dup → [:s1 :left :left] ✓ per the reviewer's in-memory probe.\n\nNote — the do-element roots: `(do (tap :left) (- n 1))` compiles to nested lambda app — distinct roots per label ✓ (they differ by the label literal).\n\nWrite the replacement now.","signature":"eda845235c3840a398547330"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"dafcc9cd-cbee-4be0-8c2b-54421f9e997c","timestamp":"2026-11-19T18:10:04.897Z","thinking_duration_ms":16348,"thinking_display":"updates"}
